# phantom/data holds two DIFFERENT things: runtime state (threat-intel cache,
# generated artifacts) that must not be committed, and PRODUCT ASSETS (the
# report templates the renderer loads BY NAME) that must be. Ignoring the
# whole directory looked harmless and was not: the template existed on the
# developer's disk and in no clone, so every report test passed locally and
# the unit-test step failed on CI for months with "Template not found".
# `phantom/data/*` + a negation keeps the state ignored and the assets tracked.
phantom/data/*
!phantom/data/templates/
!phantom/data/templates/**

