# ── Runtime output the operator generates by USING the tool ────────────────
# Phantom is meant to be run from inside the operator's working copy, so a
# normal session writes engagement material into data/. These are wholesale
# DIRECTORY ignores, not per-file patterns: a new artefact type must not be
# able to leak just because nobody listed its extension. An `git add -A` in a
# tool that handles engagement data is how a customer's targets, credentials
# and loot end up in a public repository — see CONTRIBUTING.md.
# The committed templates under data/ (persistence_rules.json.sample,
# presets/.gitkeep, wordlists/custom/.gitkeep) stay tracked; nothing else in
# these trees is source.
data/beacons/
data/drivers/
data/ransom_sim/
data/trojan/
data/sessions/
data/social_attachments/
# HID / DuckyScript payload vectors generated by `payload hid`
# (e.g. data/vectors/pico_main.py): generated device source, not this repo
data/vectors/
# Any wordlist the module downloads, scrapes or builds — every flavour, so a
# new one cannot leak by having an extension nobody listed.
data/wordlists/**
!data/wordlists/custom/
!data/wordlists/custom/.gitkeep

# OSINT output dumped into the working copy (username -> social profiles)
someuser.txt
# A crashed `use exploit` test used to leave its scratch file in the payload
# tree; the test now uses a temp dir, this is the belt-and-braces.
/phantom/exploits/test/demo.py
